>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_looper`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_looper :
  string * (simpset -> tactic) -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Replaces all tactic loopers in a simpset with one named looper.

A call to `set_looper (name, make_tac) ss` returns a new simpset whose
looper list consists only of `(name, make_tac)`.  Rewrite rules, safe and
unsafe solvers, and the other simpset strategy settings are unchanged.
The replacement is recorded as a strategy update and survives later
rebuilding of the simpset from fragment history.

The supplied function receives the active simpset and returns a tactic.
After rewriting and final solving fail, that tactic is tried.  On
success the simplifier restarts rewriting, solving, and looping on every
resulting subgoal.  The tactic must fail when inapplicable and must not
succeed without progress; otherwise an unlimited simpset can loop.  A
`Conv.UNCHANGED` exception is treated as tactic failure.

`set_looper` discards registration order because it creates a singleton
list.  A later `add_looper` with a different name appends after this
looper; a later addition with the same name updates it in place.

The bound set by `simpLib.limit n` permits at most `n` successful looper
rounds during one top-level simplification-tactic call, shared over all
subgoals.  `Excl name` in a theorem-list argument temporarily suppresses
the singleton looper, without changing the simpset returned here.

Loopers belong to the tactic layer used by `GEN_SIMP_TAC` and its
clients.  They are not invoked by `SIMP_CONV`, `SIMP_PROVE`, `SIMP_RULE`,
or `ASM_SIMP_RULE`.

### Failure

`set_looper` itself never fails and does not run the supplied function.
A later simplification tactic may diverge if the looper repeatedly
succeeds without progress and no finite limit is installed.

### Example

``` hol4
val conjunction_only =
  simpLib.set_looper
    ("split conjunctions", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
    an_existing_simpset
```

The result has no loopers inherited from `an_existing_simpset`; only
`"split conjunctions"` remains.

